619
01:29:09,588 --> 01:29:18,968
Now, if you write a synchronized keyword here, only one thread can execute this method at a time.

620
01:29:19,296 --> 01:29:43,615
Okay, so if you write a synchronized method, for example, to this method, in that case, what will happen is that, so when the LS thread comes here, when it executes the withdraw method, the second one will wait until the first thread finishes the withdraw method altogether.

621
01:29:44,275 --> 01:29:50,295
